# Generated docs collide on nearly every CLI-touching PR (two PRs each adding a
# `t3` subcommand touch adjacent lines of the same generated list), and the right
# resolution is a re-run of the file's generator. A merge driver cannot be that
# re-run — it runs before git writes any of the merge result to the working tree, so
# it would regenerate from the ours side and record that as a clean merge. The
# `generated` driver (scripts/hooks/git_merge_generated.py) therefore merges these
# paths exactly as an unregistered clone does and warns on stderr that they must be
# regenerated after the merge. See souliane/teatree#4259 and souliane/teatree#3582.
docs/generated/cli-reference.md merge=generated
docs/generated/antipattern-catalog.md merge=generated
docs/generated/management-commands.md merge=generated
evals/README.md merge=generated
